	<p>&nbsp;</p>
	<blockquote>
	<font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="+1" color="#333333"><b>Guidelines of Conduct</b></font><br>
	<font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1">
	<P>Your actions reflect on all others who wear the tag of the Sangreal</P>
	<P>As a guild, the Sangreal acknowledges the published "Play Nice 
	Rules" of Mystic as the basic guideline for the conduct of the members of the 
	guild.</P>
	<P>As member of Sangreal you should always respect another player's character. 
	Name-calling and other disparaging remarks towards another bring no honor upon 
	oneself. If you do have a serious problem with another player, it is appropriate 
	to bring this to the attention of the officers of the guild. It's important to 
	remember that the services of another guild member are not owed to you. Remember 
	the other guild members are here to play too. Its unfair to expect them to drop 
	everything and help you, they may have a commitment to their current group. 
	Please remember, when you ask -- you are asking for a favor and that player has 
	a right to say no.</P>
	<P>A Sangreal member's word is their honor, in any world. If you tell a guild 
	member, or anyone for that matter, that you will assist them. Do it. Respect 
	their time in this world, once you give your word to assist them -- get there. 
	Do as you said you would. Uphold your word, it is one of the most valuable 
	things here.</P>
	<font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="+1" color="#333333"><b>Expectations of Participation</b></font><br>
	<P>The participation of its members is vital to the survival of the guild. 
	Loyalty and Commitment are core values and the guild feels that these values 
	reflect themselves in participation in guild events. </P>
	<P>Sangreal has the expectation that a member will participate in 
	approximately 40% of the events the guild stages. Failure to maintain this level 
	of participation can result in a member's status being set to inactive. The 
	guild's Council on a quarterly basis will assess level of participation for 
	the membership.</P>
	<P>In addition to meeting the requirements for membership, players are expected 
	to maintain current information on their guilded characters on the guild's 
	website. Failure to maintain current information may lead to a player's status 
	to be set to inactive.</P></FONT>
	<font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="+1" color="#333333"><b>Violations </b></font><br>
	<P>
	<UL><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1">
	<LI>Harassment. Overt and unwanted communication of a sexual nature. No dirty 
	talk if there is any chance of offending someone. 
	<LI>Excessive Begging, Sangreal members are a very generous and giving group 
	of players. Abuse of this generosity through excessive requests for items, 
	platinum or services is grounds for a legitimate complaint that could lead to a 
	player's removal from the guild. 
	<LI>Kill Stealing. If an area or spawn is being camped please respect the 
	priority of those players. If an area has been broken and is under the control 
	of another group, respect their rights to exploit their efforts. Scams. Trying 
	to cheat another player or the game. 
	<LI>Intentional Training. This will get you banned from the game. If a situation 
	develops where you are not having fun then leave that area and go somewhere you 
	will.</LI></UL></font>
	</P></FONT>
	<font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="+1" color="#333333"><b>Removal From the 
	Guild</b></font><br>
	<font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1">
	<P>A player may be removed from the guild under the following circumstances.</P>
	<P>Administrative Removal A player may be removed from the roster of Sangreal upon the request of the player. A player may be removed from the 
	roster of the Sangreal when their guild status has remained inactive 
	for 2 quarters.</P>
	<P>Disciplinary Removal If a player consistently and willfully behaves in a 
	manner that is contrary to the spirit of the guidelines of the charter of the 
	Sangreal they may be removed from the guild. To be removed, a player 
	must have a formal grievance filed against them. Grievances may be filed via 
	e-mail. The grievance must supply sufficient detail for verification. A player 
	with a grievance will be notified of the grievance within 7 days of the original 
	receipt. The player will be informed of the nature of the complaint and the 
	identity of the player filing the grievance. The Guild will attempt 
	determine the facts and present his findings to the guild officers. If 75% of 
	the officers with an active status concur, the player will be removed from the 
	guild. Guild officers, including the leader, are not exempt from grievances. 
	</P></FONT>

</font>
	
